Adds something codebase-design has no measure for: which functions belong together before a seam is cut. It scores each coupled pair on Khononov's integration strength, distance and volatility (BALANCE = (STRENGTH XOR DISTANCE) OR NOT VOLATILITY; MAINTENANCE_EFFORT = STRENGTH x DISTANCE x VOLATILITY), classifies pairs from CRITICAL to GOOD, and estimates volatility from git co-change. Limits for this task:
- its distance scale and heuristics are service-scale (different services, deployment and team coordination);
- it uses component and service terms that codebase-design's glossary forbids;
- per-file co-change degenerates inside one file, so function-level history is needed;
- it asks the user for business context or infers it from code;
- the file last changed 2026-02-26, and no upstream evals were found.
